Andrew Fenton <andrewafenton@removethis.yahoo.com> writes:
> How does the game determine what a wizard's second starting
> spellbook is?  It seems to be weighted towards lower level
> spells: is this because such spellbooks are more common, because
> of the shallow dungeon level, or a separate calculation?  And is
> there a spoiler with the chances of starting with a particular
> spellbook?

Not weighted towards: constrained to. Starting spellbooks will always
be level 3 or less, never be a duplicate, and always be of a school
that the role is unrestricted in (so, any, for Wizards). "/* powerful
spells are either useless to low level players or unbalancing; also
spells in restricted skill categories */" is the relevant source
comment.

Under those constraints, the relative probabilities for random
spellbooks (those issued to Priests, and one of those issued to
Wizards) are those listed in spl1-342.txt.

